IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tcpss-customer`

-- Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999 -- worked cases, from the seat of the phone
-- customer. Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written
-- by hand from the deposited text (Compilation No. 45), never copied from the encoding's output. All facts are
-- HYPOTHETICAL; no scenario raised this Act.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The universal service obligation. A farmer near Kununurra asks for a fixed line; no Ministerial instruments in play.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a standard telephone service` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the primary universal service provider for my area must supply me a standard telephone service on request (s 9(1)(a), (2), s 12C)`
-- She has not yet asked.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a standard telephone service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a request is needed; the obligation is to supply on request (s 9(2))`
-- Her request does not meet the Minister's s 9(2D) requirements.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a standard telephone service` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: my request does not comply with the requirements the Minister has determined under s 9(2D) (s 9(2C))`
-- Her circumstances are excluded by a s 9(3) determination.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a standard telephone service` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: my circumstances are ones the Minister has determined under s 9(3) in which the obligation does not arise (s 9(2E))`
-- A s 8J declaration has taken effect: no obligation, whatever else.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a standard telephone service` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the Minister's s 8J declaration that there are satisfactory alternative contractual arrangements has survived disallowance (s 9(2AAA))`
-- Asking from a place outside Australia.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a standard telephone service` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the obligation is to people in Australia, where they reside or carry on business (s 9(1)(a))`

-- Who supplies it: no s 12A determination for her area: Telstra (s 12D(1)).
#ASSERT `Who must supply my standard telephone service` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Telstra Limited, which is taken to be the primary universal service provider outside a special determined area (s 12D(1))`
#ASSERT `Who must supply my standard telephone service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the one provider the Minister has determined for my area (ss 12A(1), 12C(1))`
#ASSERT `Who must supply my standard telephone service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `each of the providers the Minister has determined for my area; any one of them may supply it (ss 12A(2A), 12C(2))`

-- Equipment: a handset with no switching functions, to hire if she prefers (ss 9E(1)(b), 9(6)).
#ASSERT `What equipment must come with my service` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a telephone handset without switching functions, with the option of hiring it (ss 9E(1)(b), 9(6))`
-- A deaf customer for whom voice telephony is not practical: the equipment the Disability Discrimination Act requires.
#ASSERT `What equipment must come with my service` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the equipment the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 requires instead of a handset (for example a text telephone), with the option of hiring it (ss 6(1)(b), 9E(1), 9(6))`
#ASSERT `What equipment must come with my service` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the customer equipment the regulations prescribe, with the option of hiring it (ss 9E(1)(a), 9(6))`
-- She has her own phone and asks not to be given one.
#ASSERT `What equipment must come with my service` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none: I asked not to be supplied with it, so the obligation does not extend to it (s 9(4))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Untimed local calls. Inputs: standard zone; residential or charity; voice calls; within the local zone; an old untimed
-- kind or a universal service; a mobile or satellite party outside the universal service; the provider charges for them.
-- A household in a Perth suburb calling a neighbour on the fixed line.
#ASSERT `Must my provider offer untimed local calls` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- A business: also fine for voice calls ...
#ASSERT `Must my provider offer untimed local calls` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- ... but not for data calls (s 106(2)(a)); a household's data calls still count (s 106(1)).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must my provider offer untimed local calls` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `Must my provider offer untimed local calls` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- A call to a mobile phone that is not a universal service: not an eligible local call.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must my provider offer untimed local calls` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
-- A call outside the local zone.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must my provider offer untimed local calls` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
-- A customer outside any standard zone (s 107's scheme is for the regulations).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must my provider offer untimed local calls` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))

-- How the calls may be charged. Inputs: chose untimed on connection; later gave written notice; since consented otherwise.
#ASSERT `How may my local calls be charged` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `untimed only: my provider may not charge them any other way without my written consent (s 105(1)(b), (d)(ii))`
#ASSERT `How may my local calls be charged` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `untimed from the earliest practicable period after my provider receives my notice, and not otherwise without my written consent (s 105(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `How may my local calls be charged` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my provider may charge them another way, but I may give written notice at any time that I want them untimed (s 105(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `How may my local calls be charged` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my provider may charge them another way, but I may give written notice at any time that I want them untimed (s 105(1)(c))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The customer service guarantee. A repair is late (a contravention of the ACMA's standard, as a fact).
#ASSERT `Am I owed damages under the customer service guarantee` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my provider is liable to pay me damages for the contravention (s 116(1))`
-- She had signed a valid waiver for a non-universal service.
#ASSERT `Am I owed damages under the customer service guarantee` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I validly waived the customer service guarantee for this service (s 120(2))`
-- A waiver signed for a universal service line does not count (s 120(7)).
#ASSERT `Am I owed damages under the customer service guarantee` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: my provider is liable to pay me damages for the contravention (s 116(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I owed damages under the customer service guarantee` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the standard does not apply to my provider at my location, because it does not supply or offer that kind of service there (s 115(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I owed damages under the customer service guarantee` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: my provider has not contravened a performance standard in relation to me`

-- The amount: a hypothetical scale amount of $120, less a $20 goodwill credit for the same fault (s 116(3)).
#ASSERT `How much guarantee damages must my provider pay` 120 20 EQUALS `answered` 100
#ASSERT `How much guarantee damages must my provider pay` 120 0 EQUALS `answered` 120
-- A $150 credit already given: not below zero.
#ASSERT `How much guarantee damages must my provider pay` 120 150 EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `How much guarantee damages must my provider pay` 30000 0 EQUALS `not covered` `the scale of damages may not specify more than $25,000 for a category (s 117(3)): an amount above that is not a valid scale amount`

-- The repair period was missed from 3 March 2026 and the fault continued: sue by 3 March 2028 (s 116(6)(a)).
#ASSERT `The last day to sue for guarantee damages` (Date 3 3 2026) EQUALS Date 3 3 2028
-- The provider had reason to believe on 3 March 2026: it must decide by 17 March 2026 (s 117A(1)).
#ASSERT `The last day for my provider to decide on liability` (Date 3 3 2026) EQUALS Date 17 3 2026
-- It decided on 10 March 2026: pay or credit, or tell her it will not, within 14 weeks, by 16 June 2026 (s 117A(3)-(5)).
#ASSERT `The last day for my provider to pay or tell me` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 16 6 2026

#ASSERT `Can my provider make me waive the guarantee` TRUE EQUALS `no: I cannot waive my protection and rights under Part 5 for a universal service phone line (s 120(7))`
#ASSERT `Can my provider make me waive the guarantee` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my provider may make supply conditional on a waiver (s 120A), but the waiver must follow the ACMA's rules and form, with a statement of its consequences, and cannot be in the provider's standard form of agreement (s 120(3)-(6))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The Ombudsman. Inputs: a carrier; fixed phone to homes or small businesses; mobile; internet; directed; exempted.
-- A mobile reseller with no network of its own.
#ASSERT `Must my provider be in the Ombudsman scheme` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is an eligible carriage service provider, and must enter into the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman scheme (ss 127, 128(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my provider be in the Ombudsman scheme` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is an eligible carriage service provider, and must enter into the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman scheme (ss 127, 128(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my provider be in the Ombudsman scheme` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a carrier, and must enter into the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman scheme (s 128(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my provider be in the Ombudsman scheme` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the ACMA has declared it exempt (s 129)`
-- A provider of a fixed line only to large businesses, not directed: not required.
#ASSERT `Must my provider be in the Ombudsman scheme` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act does not require it to join, though membership must be open to it (s 128(7))`
#ASSERT `Must my provider be in the Ombudsman scheme` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the ACMA has directed it, or its class, to enter into the scheme (ss 130, 131)`

#ASSERT `Can the Ombudsman take my complaint` `billing, or the manner of charging` EQUALS `yes: the scheme must provide for the Ombudsman to investigate, determine and give directions on it, and my provider may not charge me for my complaint (s 128(4), (4A), (5))`
#ASSERT `Can the Ombudsman take my complaint` `the service itself (a fault, a connection, the supply)` EQUALS `yes: the scheme must provide for the Ombudsman to investigate, determine and give directions on it, and my provider may not charge me for my complaint (s 128(4), (4A), (5))`
#ASSERT `Can the Ombudsman take my complaint` `the level at which the provider's prices are set` EQUALS `no: the scheme must not provide for the Ombudsman to investigate it (s 128(6))`
#ASSERT `Can the Ombudsman take my complaint` `the content of a content service` EQUALS `no: the scheme must not provide for the Ombudsman to investigate it (s 128(6))`
#ASSERT `Can the Ombudsman take my complaint` `the connection of my premises by a statutory infrastructure provider` EQUALS `perhaps: the scheme may provide for the Ombudsman to deal with it, but the Act does not require it (s 128(5A))`
